<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Plutonic takes stake in gold explorer.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Plutonic takes stake in gold explorer.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold miner Plutonic Resources Ltd said on Tuesday it had bought an 8.94 percent stake in gold explorer North Star Resources NL.</p>
<p>Plutonic said in a substantial shareholder notice to the Australian Stock Exchange (ASX) that it holds 12.0 million North Star shares.</p>
<p>At 11.05 a.m. (0105 GMT), North Star shares were 0.5 cents lower at 12 cents. Based on this price, Plutonic's investment in North Star is worth A$1.44 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
